{
  "$comment": "Single source of truth for material identity, shared by JS and C++. Edit here, then run `npm run generate` to regenerate materials.generated.js and cpp/engine/materials.generated.hpp. Numeric ids MUST stay stable: saved scenes, worldgen, tests, and the WASM grid key off them. `flags` and `componentGroup` make material behavior class-based: predicates (isFlammable/isDissolvable/isRigidMaterial/isBearingMaterial/isPlantMaterial) and component registration are generated from these, so a new material that reuses existing physics needs only a schema entry.",
  "tableSize": 32,
  "kinds": {
    "NONE": 0,
    "POWDER": 1,
    "LIQUID": 2,
    "GAS": 3,
    "COMPONENT": 4,
    "FREE_RIGID": 5
  },
  "$flagDoc": "Bit index per behavior flag. flammable: ignites near fire/lava. dissolvable: acid eats it. rigid: a solid that grounds via rigid contact + is moved by moveRigidAssemblies. bearing: supports loose material above it (rigid ∪ sand-like powders). plantFamily: belongs to the growable plant-component family (flooded unbounded; fire-split).",
  "flagBits": {
    "flammable": 0,
    "dissolvable": 1,
    "rigid": 2,
    "bearing": 3,
    "plantFamily": 4
  },
  "$cgroupDoc": "Which seeded-component list a material registers into (registerSeededComponents). none: not a seeded component (powders, liquids, gases, free-rigid bodies). stone: chunk-bounded flood, one island per same-id region (ores included). plant: unbounded flood (a whole tree is one comp). ice: unbounded flood.",
  "componentGroups": {
    "none": 0,
    "stone": 1,
    "plant": 2,
    "ice": 3
  },
